          {
            "commit": "c926c83e27c6c7a8c3a92cc508b8e0a3ad647ac3",
            "subject": "LU-20424 ldiskfs: save dirdata in ext4_htree_store_dirent"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-07-21 21:58:27.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-07-21 22:36:58.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20424 ldiskfs: save dirdata in dirent for 6.18/7.0",
        "message": "LU-20424 ldiskfs: save dirdata in dirent for 6.18/7.0\n\next4_htree_store_dirent() saves direntries to return in hash order,\nbut didn't take dirdata into account, so OSD couldn't find any FIDs.\n\n    osd_fid_unpack()) unexpected packed fid size: 0\n    osd_fid_unpack()) Skipped 14381 previous similar messages\n\nAdd a simple test to check for FIDs in dir entries.\n\nFix ldiskfs-6.18 patch to address this issue, and create a new\nldiskfs-7.0 patch due to changes in this area.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 409935cc7094 (\"LU-19847 ldiskfs: dirent and fscrypt+case_insensitive\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I3eaf89606aece19fdb0ae35e846406d15c3ebbe5\n"
      },
